WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.074 --> 00:00:03.079
- Triple-decker hamburger
made out of a doughnut.

00:00:03.079 --> 00:00:04.920
I'm going to make Steve eat one of those.

00:00:05.413 --> 00:00:07.033
Steve's going to eat a
triple-decker hamburger

00:00:07.033 --> 00:00:08.310
out of a doughnut.

00:00:09.942 --> 00:00:14.546
(upbeat music)

00:00:14.583 --> 00:00:17.127
- All right, where are we going, Colin?

00:00:17.127 --> 00:00:19.402
- We're going to the
Los Angeles County Fair.

00:00:19.402 --> 00:00:21.480
- Are you going to win me a prize?

00:00:23.981 --> 00:00:24.643
Excited?

00:00:24.643 --> 00:00:25.479
- [Colin] I'm excited.

00:00:25.479 --> 00:00:26.164
- [Freddie] Whoo!

00:00:26.164 --> 00:00:27.348
- [Steven] Oh my God!

00:00:27.348 --> 00:00:29.669
- I already see, like,
nine things I want to eat.

00:00:29.669 --> 00:00:33.728
- Doughnuts, cookie dough, now you know.

00:00:33.728 --> 00:00:34.993
- We're going to play a
little game of telephone.

00:00:34.993 --> 00:00:36.096
We're going to go to one booth,

00:00:36.096 --> 00:00:37.453
- Eat that amazing food,

00:00:37.453 --> 00:00:38.894
ask them what their favorite booth is,

00:00:38.894 --> 00:00:39.788
go to that booth,

00:00:39.788 --> 00:00:41.575
- And then we're going to go
on, and on, and on, and on,

00:00:41.575 --> 00:00:42.725
- And by the end of this,

00:00:42.725 --> 00:00:45.825
I plan to have what everybody
has at the end of a fair,

00:00:45.825 --> 00:00:48.205
a sunburn and a stomach ache.

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:49.536
- Let's go!

00:00:49.536 --> 00:00:52.021
- Our fair chaperon suggested
we start at Chicken Charlie's,

00:00:52.021 --> 00:00:54.157
which sounds fine to me,
I always can eat chicken.

00:00:54.157 --> 00:00:55.318
And look at that booth!

00:00:55.318 --> 00:00:56.641
Woah!

00:00:56.641 --> 00:00:59.114
I think we have to get a
Totally Fried Guacamole,

00:00:59.114 --> 00:01:00.681
the triple-decker burger,

00:01:00.681 --> 00:01:03.153
and I think we need some fried Oreos, too.

00:01:03.153 --> 00:01:04.094
- [Steven] Are we going to eat all that?

00:01:04.094 --> 00:01:04.883
- [Colin] Yeah!

00:01:04.883 --> 00:01:06.958
- We're at booth number one guys.

00:01:06.958 --> 00:01:07.790
- Fried guac

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:10.375
- Oh my god!
- Fried guacamole is awesome.

00:01:10.375 --> 00:01:12.037
- It's literally just guacamole

00:01:12.037 --> 00:01:14.510
with a layer of dough around it.

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:15.728
- It's kinda healthy, right?

00:01:15.728 --> 00:01:18.015
- The crispness of the fried batter

00:01:18.015 --> 00:01:19.409
is really, really on point.

00:01:19.409 --> 00:01:22.092
- This is maybe the grossest
concoction I've ever seen,

00:01:22.092 --> 00:01:23.113
and I love it.

00:01:23.113 --> 00:01:25.956
- Triple-decker burger
with Steven's favorite,

00:01:25.956 --> 00:01:27.629
Krispy Kreme doughnuts.

00:01:27.629 --> 00:01:30.576
- Glazed, I don't need you
anymore Freddie, I've got this.

00:01:30.576 --> 00:01:33.874
- It's sweet, it's savory, it
tastes like a heart attack.

00:01:33.874 --> 00:01:36.568
- The meat and the doughnut
are the same texture.

00:01:36.568 --> 00:01:38.599
I will say this is a
balanced meal, though.

00:01:38.599 --> 00:01:41.383
Like we have the meat,
we have the veggies,

00:01:41.383 --> 00:01:42.550
and now dessert.

00:01:42.550 --> 00:01:43.642
- I'm not mad at it.

00:01:43.642 --> 00:01:45.462
- Wow.
- I love it.

00:01:45.466 --> 00:01:47.460
- I was expecting, like,
to crunch into the Oreo,

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:50.454
but look at that, they
somehow made the Oreo

00:01:50.454 --> 00:01:53.323
into a soft, gushy, pleasant surprise.

00:01:53.323 --> 00:01:55.899
- If you were a 10 year old,
which would be your favorite?

00:01:55.899 --> 00:01:57.505
- [Steve] Fried Oreos.
- [Freddie] Fried Oreos.

00:01:57.505 --> 00:01:59.595
- If I was 10, I still
think Fried Guacamole

00:01:59.595 --> 00:02:00.698
would be my favorite.

00:02:00.698 --> 00:02:02.044
- You were one of those kids.

00:02:02.044 --> 00:02:03.484
- 10 on the 10-year-old scale for sure.

00:02:03.484 --> 00:02:04.562
- Totally.

00:02:04.562 --> 00:02:06.688
- Heart attack variable, 10.

00:02:06.688 --> 00:02:08.131
- Yeah, I'm going to have
one in, like, 20 minutes.

00:02:08.131 --> 00:02:09.350
- 11.

00:02:09.350 --> 00:02:10.204
- Creativity?

00:02:10.204 --> 00:02:11.988
- I give them an eight.

00:02:11.988 --> 00:02:13.827
- Total score 28 out of 30.

00:02:13.827 --> 00:02:15.846
Almost perfect, but we can get better.

00:02:15.846 --> 00:02:20.191
- If you weren't going
to eat at your booth,

00:02:20.191 --> 00:02:21.990
what other booth at the fair,

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:24.371
do you think would be where
you would get your food?

00:02:24.371 --> 00:02:28.572
- I keep hearing a lot
about fried watermelon.

00:02:28.572 --> 00:02:32.531
I do not know exactly
the name of the place.

00:02:32.531 --> 00:02:36.137
- A fair legend, I like it,
okay, fried watermelon it is.

00:02:36.688 --> 00:02:40.211
(upbeat fair music)

00:02:40.211 --> 00:02:41.371
- [Steven] You alright there?

00:02:41.371 --> 00:02:43.135
- Yeah, just covering up.

00:02:43.135 --> 00:02:45.027
It's like the Sahara out here.

00:02:45.027 --> 00:02:48.626
- We're on the hunt for the
booth with the fried watermelon.

00:02:48.626 --> 00:02:49.694
We don't know the name of the booth,

00:02:49.694 --> 00:02:51.147
we're just rolling with the punches,

00:02:51.147 --> 00:02:52.654
seeing what we stumble upon.

00:02:52.654 --> 00:02:54.469
- Do you guys have fried watermelon?

00:02:54.469 --> 00:02:56.763
- Argh!

00:02:56.763 --> 00:02:59.643
We're going to have three
sticks of fried watermelon?

00:03:01.992 --> 00:03:03.594
Should we get pineapple, too, guys?

00:03:03.594 --> 00:03:05.219
- [Colln] Let's do two
watermelons, one pineapple.

00:03:05.219 --> 00:03:08.120
- [Woman] The best upside-down pineapple.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:09.390
- That is crazy!

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:11.249
- [Woman] Here is the
queen of the deep fried,

00:03:11.249 --> 00:03:13.590
it's the deep-fried watermelon.

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:16.118
- [Freddie] I don't even have words.

00:03:16.118 --> 00:03:17.265
- Fried watermelon?

00:03:17.265 --> 00:03:19.264
It's like, you'd think
it would melt, right?

00:03:19.264 --> 00:03:21.237
- No, still super fresh, still--

00:03:21.237 --> 00:03:22.503
- They picked this
watermelon out yesterday.

00:03:22.503 --> 00:03:23.408
This is fried pizza.

00:03:23.408 --> 00:03:24.557
- Cheers guys.

00:03:25.215 --> 00:03:26.213
- [Steven] That's how you make pizza.

00:03:26.213 --> 00:03:26.968
- [Colin] Uh huh.

00:03:26.968 --> 00:03:28.106
- [Steven] Why is this not done more?

00:03:28.106 --> 00:03:29.753
- That's weird, I like it.

00:03:29.753 --> 00:03:30.671
- [Freddie] Super flaky.

00:03:30.671 --> 00:03:32.053
- It has the taste of a pizza,

00:03:32.053 --> 00:03:33.793
and the texture of a glazed doughnut.

00:03:33.793 --> 00:03:35.429
- If I was 10, I would love this.

00:03:35.429 --> 00:03:36.305
- Heart attack,

00:03:36.305 --> 00:03:38.325
this is not going to
send you to the hospital.

00:03:38.325 --> 00:03:39.172
- Six

00:03:39.172 --> 00:03:40.810
- Creativity, I give it an eight.

00:03:40.810 --> 00:03:42.040
- Yeah, I mean, it's pizza, fried.

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:45.349
10 plus six, plus eight, is 24.

00:03:45.349 --> 00:03:46.835
We gotta ask them where we're going next.

00:03:46.835 --> 00:03:50.248
- If you're not eating
at your own lovely booth,

00:03:50.248 --> 00:03:52.767
where else in the LA County
Fair do you like to eat?

00:03:52.767 --> 00:03:54.950
- Well, let's see, we'll eat at Pepe's,

00:03:54.950 --> 00:03:56.727
which is over on Palm.

00:03:56.727 --> 00:03:57.434
- [Steven] You ready?

00:03:57.434 --> 00:03:58.661
- Pepe's it is, let's go!

00:03:58.661 --> 00:03:59.666
- [Steven] Go.

00:04:00.333 --> 00:04:01.494
You guys are standing there, let's go.

00:04:01.494 --> 00:04:03.793
- Hi, I'm Lola. The number
one item that I sell,

00:04:03.793 --> 00:04:05.917
I started with the fish
tacos, the grilled fish tacos.

00:04:05.917 --> 00:04:08.135
It's healthy, guilt-free.

00:04:08.135 --> 00:04:10.200
- This straw is for Steve,
I don't want his cooties.

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:10.602
- [Steven] You guys ready?

00:04:10.602 --> 00:04:11.903
This is like Taco Truck all over again.

00:04:11.903 --> 00:04:14.526
- Day one guys, it's a throwback.

00:04:14.526 --> 00:04:16.650
This taco is for you, Andrew.

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:19.623
(inspirational music)

00:04:19.623 --> 00:04:22.027
- Cheers, Colin you always jump the gun.

00:04:22.027 --> 00:04:23.844
- I always forget the cheers.

00:04:23.844 --> 00:04:24.665
- Yes!

00:04:24.665 --> 00:04:26.127
- The best part, not fried.

00:04:26.127 --> 00:04:27.300
- [Steven] If I worked at the fair,

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:28.206
I'd probably eat here a lot.

00:04:28.206 --> 00:04:29.727
You just get so tired
of all the fried food.

00:04:29.727 --> 00:04:31.190
- You don't get tired of fried food,

00:04:31.190 --> 00:04:33.267
you just have to stop
eating it or you'll die.

00:04:33.267 --> 00:04:35.798
- This place gave me a
whole new pep in my step.

00:04:35.798 --> 00:04:38.004
I was starting to feel a
little weak at one point.

00:04:38.004 --> 00:04:39.990
- Yeah this is a good,
like, palate cleanser.

00:04:39.990 --> 00:04:41.987
I think our rubric should be scratched.

00:04:41.987 --> 00:04:43.066
This is our intermission.

00:04:43.066 --> 00:04:45.167
- Because on the heart
attack scale, it gets a one.

00:04:45.167 --> 00:04:46.827
- And you don't need a heart
attack to have a good time.

00:04:46.827 --> 00:04:49.486
- We were told that the best
funnel cake at the fair,

00:04:49.486 --> 00:04:51.159
is at the Mad Hatter.

00:04:52.109 --> 00:04:54.206
- Funnel cake, scary animal, let's go.

00:04:54.206 --> 00:04:58.351
- We're gonna get one Holy
Moly Double-decker Funnel Cake.

00:04:58.351 --> 00:05:00.824
We got chocolate-dipped bacon,

00:05:00.824 --> 00:05:04.203
and a double-decker funnel
cake with strawberries.

00:05:04.203 --> 00:05:05.747
- [Freddie] This is my cutie for the day.

00:05:05.747 --> 00:05:06.803
- What is going on?

00:05:06.803 --> 00:05:07.871
- Cheers, guys.

00:05:07.871 --> 00:05:09.416
- What do you know
about chocolate, Steven?

00:05:09.416 --> 00:05:11.413
- I know absolutely nothing.

00:05:11.413 --> 00:05:12.413
- I'm not a fan.

00:05:12.413 --> 00:05:14.771
- Me neither. (laughs)

00:05:14.771 --> 00:05:16.696
- It just tastes like
chocolate-covered paper.

00:05:16.696 --> 00:05:17.719
- Ew.

00:05:17.719 --> 00:05:18.577
- It's not bad.

00:05:18.577 --> 00:05:20.773
- Funnel cake, it's why
they invented the fair.

00:05:20.773 --> 00:05:22.988
We're going to give you a heart attack.

00:05:22.988 --> 00:05:24.154
- This isn't your normal funnel cake.

00:05:24.154 --> 00:05:25.380
- Nope.
- It's so light.

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:26.785
- It's not actually a heart attack.

00:05:26.785 --> 00:05:28.132
- It's not crazy sweet.

00:05:28.132 --> 00:05:29.513
- It's starting to look
like a heart attack though.

00:05:29.513 --> 00:05:30.489
That's for sure.

00:05:30.489 --> 00:05:32.196
- 10-year-old factor, this is a 10.

00:05:32.196 --> 00:05:33.172
- This is a 20.
- 10.

00:05:33.172 --> 00:05:35.811
- You find me a 10 year old
who doesn't like funnel cake,

00:05:35.811 --> 00:05:39.421
I'll show you a very, very sad kid.

00:05:39.421 --> 00:05:40.245
- Creativity?

00:05:40.245 --> 00:05:41.301
- It's sort of light and feathery.

00:05:41.301 --> 00:05:42.023
- It's different.

00:05:42.023 --> 00:05:43.326
- And it's also a double decker.

00:05:43.326 --> 00:05:44.522
Which adds a new element.

00:05:44.522 --> 00:05:45.357
- For me, nine.

00:05:45.357 --> 00:05:46.454
It's a visual heart attack,

00:05:46.454 --> 00:05:48.937
wasn't exactly a heart attack though.

00:05:48.937 --> 00:05:51.170
Fried guacamole, that was a heart attack.

00:05:51.170 --> 00:05:52.458
This is, yeah, like a seven.

00:05:52.458 --> 00:05:53.857
26.
- Yeah.

00:05:53.857 --> 00:05:54.902
- Really good.

00:05:54.902 --> 00:05:56.006
- Solid score, funnel cake.

00:05:56.006 --> 00:05:57.271
We made it.
- We made it.

00:05:57.271 --> 00:05:58.652
- We made it.
- LA County Fair.

00:05:58.652 --> 00:06:00.174
- We learned that the fair

00:06:00.174 --> 00:06:01.915
is a great place to go once a year.

00:06:01.915 --> 00:06:03.251
You go more than once a year,

00:06:03.251 --> 00:06:04.110
you'll be on your back.

00:06:04.110 --> 00:06:06.080
- I'm going to explode
right now, actually.

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:09.139
- Should we get some more,
uh, fried guac on the way out?

00:06:09.139 --> 00:06:10.080
- Yes!

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:11.868
Peace.

00:06:11.868 --> 00:06:16.633
(jazzy upbeat music)

00:06:17.132 --> 00:06:19.268
- You do not want me behind
the wheel of a car right now.

